From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:19:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C7 GMAT: compare a text-report readout with SPICE printed at
 the same precision

NAMING.md records the 8-9 November amendment, written before any real GMAT SPK comparison was seen:
for a tool whose only readout is a fixed-precision text report, its states are compared with
SPICE's evaluation of the same kernel printed at the same precision, so both pass through the same
readout; the bar is unchanged. Reason: a stand-in returning SPICE's own states fails the rule as
first written through GMAT's 16-digit report (2.18e-11 km against 1.46e-11 km). It applies to GMAT
only; Orekit, Basilisk and ANISE keep the full-double comparison.

kshana_fd.evaluated_compare takes readout_digits (default None, the full-double comparison);
gmat_reader.REPORT_DIGITS = 16 sets both the scripts' ReportFile precision and the comparison.
RESULTS (C7) records the amendment and keeps a full-precision GMAT readout as future work.
